From 00372d6530913e82b794f802d3711db850c5436e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 23:51:46 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 35/39] v4.8-gpu: cap the GPU coupling reduction and fix the
 penalty comment

The CPU-to-GPU coupling fold reduced an entity's vruntime growth by
50% per interactive signal (futex_waiting and zero CPU EMA), which with
both signals present removed 100% of the growth and froze the fold.  A
frozen fold lets an interactive entity monopolize the GPU queue because
its vruntime never advances relative to the others.  Cap the reduction
at 75% so the fold keeps growing and the queue stays fair.

While here, fix the EMA burst-penalty comment: fast submitters get the
penalty reduced by 25% (the code keeps 75%, boost -= boost >> 2), not a
quarter of it.

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/scheduler/sched_rq.c | 18 ++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/scheduler/sched_rq.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/scheduler/sched_rq.c
index f7c1ee899..832075156 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/scheduler/sched_rq.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/scheduler/sched_rq.c
@@ -278,8 +278,9 @@ static ktime_t drm_sched_entity_update_vruntime(struct drm_sched_entity *entity)
 	/* Infinity: EMA burst penalty.  Busy entities (high EMA) accrue
 	 * virtual time faster, so they drift back in the queue and the GPU
 	 * stays available to interactive entities.  Compositor-like
-	 * entities with fast submission intervals (every 1-8 ms) get only a
-	 * quarter of the penalty.
+	 * entities with fast submission intervals (every 1-8 ms) get the
+	 * burst penalty reduced by 25% (the code keeps 75% of it) so the
+	 * desktop stays smooth while batch workloads keep the full penalty.
 	 */
 	if (stats->gpu_time_ema > 0 && delta_ns > 0) {
 		u64 ema_pct = div64_u64(stats->gpu_time_ema * 100ULL,
@@ -303,7 +304,10 @@ static ktime_t drm_sched_entity_update_vruntime(struct drm_sched_entity *entity)
 	 * interactive task whose GPU submissions should not be treated as
 	 * bulk load.  Each signal halves this fold's vruntime growth, so
 	 * the entity drifts toward the front of the queue while its task
-	 * stays interactive.
+	 * stays interactive.  The reduction is capped at 75% (both signals
+	 * present) so the fold's vruntime growth never freezes -- a
+	 * fully-frozen fold would let an interactive entity monopolize the
+	 * queue.
 	 *
 	 * RCU-safe: pid_task() under rcu_read_lock() returns NULL if the
 	 * task has exited, leaving the growth unchanged.
@@ -329,9 +333,15 @@ static ktime_t drm_sched_entity_update_vruntime(struct drm_sched_entity *entity)
 		rcu_read_unlock();
 
 		if (coupling) {
-			delta_ns = delta_ns * (100 - 50 * coupling) / 100;
+			/* Cap the reduction at 75%: with both signals (coupling == 2)
+			 * the raw 100% reduction would freeze the fold's vruntime
+			 * growth and let an interactive entity monopolize the queue.
+			 */
+			u32 pct = min(50 * coupling, 75);
+
 			if (delta_ns < 0)
 				delta_ns = 0;
+			delta_ns = delta_ns * (100 - pct) / 100;
 			atomic64_inc(this_cpu_ptr(&infinity_gpu_cpu_coupling_activations));
 		}
 	}
